The guide is correct here.  If, after using everything from the main 
dungeon, the mines, the Castle, the Valley, and the Quest, the player 
doesn't have the AK, (1) he's been badly wasteful or astonishingly 
unlucky (hint: probably the former) and (2) slogging through the mazes 
with -12 AC (or whatever) is not likely to fix things.

Gehennom exists as an obstacle, not a place to obtain items.

I suppose if the player is in pretty good shape, but needs just a few 
more blank scrolls or holy water before starting the final run, he could 
levelport back to the stash for some inventory management first.

My Gehennom strategy (which I don't expect to be included in the guide):

Do the Quest
Gate to the Valley
Levelport to the VS level
Find and mark the VS
Proceed upwards with magic mapping
Find and take the portal to Rodney's
Levelport up two
Kill Rodney, take the book
Levelport to the deepest possible location for Vlad's stairs
Proceed upwards with magic mapping until they are found
Kill Vlad
Gate back to the VS level
Do invocation
Levelport down one
Get the amulet
Proceed upwards
 
